From 110ccd8746d861d0ab034fae0de4db356b180d9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:28:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kernels: second review of the computations on the device

- the thermodynamic forces in the global frame used by the inner forces
  computed by kernels are no longer copied to the host at each residual
  (updateRotatedThermodynamicForces);
- the local matrix of the prediction can't leak if its first assembly
  fails, and the elimination in the local matrix is no longer written
  twice;
- the loading function of the uniform Dirichlet boundary conditions is
  evaluated on all the processes, even without imposed degrees of
  freedom;
- documentation updated: the gradients and thermodynamic forces in the
  global frame may be computed on the device, the views of the
  behaviours integrated on the device are known to MFEM, and the
  synchronization at the beginning of a resolution.
---
 include/MFEMMGIS/BehaviourIntegratorBase.hxx  |  8 +++
 include/MFEMMGIS/Material.hxx                 |  6 +-
 include/MFEMMGIS/MaterialArrays.hxx           |  5 +-
 .../StandardBehaviourIntegratorCRTPBase.ixx   |  2 +-
 src/BehaviourIntegratorBase.cxx               | 13 +++-
 ...onLinearEvolutionProblemImplementation.cxx | 59 ++++++++++++-------
 ...nearEvolutionProblemImplementationBase.cxx |  9 +--
 src/UniformDirichletBoundaryCondition.cxx     |  6 +-
 8 files changed, 75 insertions(+), 33 deletions(-)

